# Design tokens

Tokens MUST use three tiers: primitive → semantic → component tokens.

The third tier is **component tokens** (token context only). UI modules are atoms, molecules, organisms, and templates.

UI modules and consumers MUST use semantic or component tokens. They MUST NOT use primitive tokens directly. Visual values MUST come from the token pipeline, not literals. Primitive tokens stay private.

Foundation semantic inventory:

- Color roles: `surface`, `on-surface`, `action`, `on-action`, `danger`, `on-danger`, `success`, `on-success`, `warning`, `on-warning`, `info`, `on-info`, `focus`
- Plus: space, radius, typography (Inter), density, direction (`ltr` | `rtl`)
- Schemes: light and dark in the first token drop
- Token galleries MUST show light and dark side by side

Each painted foreground/background pair MUST meet WCAG 2.2 AA contrast.

Ctrl UI identity is the CTRL monochrome lockup: ink `#000000` on cool paper near `#F2F2F2`, glint `#FFFFFF`. Action on light is ink, not a chromatic brand red. Status ramps MUST stay distinct from action.

Primitive color ramps SHOULD use stepped scales 50–900 (one hue family per ramp). Semantic roles MUST point at a step. Accent A100–A700 MUST NOT be required in this increment.

An unnamed reference product’s palette MUST NOT be copied into the default theme. It MAY be used as a theme proof. Distinct ramps are REQUIRED when a consumer brand and `danger` would otherwise share one red.

This increment ships the token pipeline. Per-atom component tokens MAY wait until the first atom.

UI typeface is Inter. Tokens MUST name family Inter. Catalog MUST load Inter via `@fontsource/inter` for weights 400, 500, 600, and 700. Do not assume Inter is installed on the OS.

This increment MUST ship direction tokens, a `dir` contract (`ltr` | `rtl`), and logical CSS for directional inset and space.
